Author: Abhinav S V <abhinavsv3@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 25 23:04:13 2026 -0700

    --jobs N: run attempts concurrently
    
    A run against a hosted model is bound by network latency, and 40 tasks
    x 3 repeats at a few minutes each was hours of a laptop doing nothing.
    
    Each attempt already had its own worktree and temp directory. What
    needed adding: a lock around git worktree add/remove, because concurrent
    adds on one repository race on .git/index.lock; one writer for the
    results file, flushed per record, so --resume still works after a kill;
    and the spend ceiling checked before each dispatch, so it is overshot by
    at most the attempts in flight. Progress prints one whole line per
    landed attempt rather than the sequential start/finish pair, which would
    interleave.
    
    --jobs 1 (the default) takes the old path and prints exactly what it
    did before. A test runs the same task set both ways and checks the
    records match.
    
    Closes #27
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

